Using 1x1 matrices for scalars would mean generalizing the way we handle
the Eigen types.  We'd want to use Eigen::Matrix<T,1,1> if we wanted to
not waste a ton of memory and cause an unacceptable amount of indirection
chasing pointers.  It could probably all be done with the kind of abstractions
that the Eigen doc discusses for return types and argument type concepts.

