I am just going through some of the arm models I have written to tidy them up before they go on github. Since a lot of the code in arm is in R, I arranged my files in the same manner as with the original bugs files. That is, I also want to rewrite the bits of R code in the book (there are a few typos which I don't want to leave unaddressed) and use rstan to allow for relatively compact code. Hereby I was wondering if there is a quick way to access generated quantities in rstan (such as model predictions). I browsed through the little guide on RStan, but could not find a quick way of doing so. I might be missing out the obvious here, but it would make some of my code a lot shorter and a lot nicer to read.

