Yikes, nesterov_gradient is all kinds of crazy.  It looks like the step size initialization routine actually performs a gradient descent and hits the optimum before a Nesterov step is even made.  Then the step function implements another step size initialization (entirely duplicated from the initialization algorithm) that infinite loops when starting at the mode.

Anyone who actually knows how this is supposed to work want to fix it?  If I don't hear from anyone by tomorrow morning I'll go ahead and clean it up while hoping I don't mess up the algorithm.

