> >
> > The basic idea is that the argument_probe class runs through the argument tree.  For each valued argument (list and singleton) it varies possible inputs (all valid values plus a "fail" value for list arguments, and good and bad values for singleton arguments that must be defined in each implementation) and then prints out the resulting tree from the original argument (all other values are set to defaults).  Tests will be broken up by the top list of arguments (method, id, data, output, random, etc).
> >
> > The tests would then take these files, convert them to an argument string (basically by removing newlines and whitespace), and then try to run them through an actual model to validate success.  I just wanted to see if you guys agreed with the general strategy or not before proceeding.  Thoughts?
