On 7/25/13 2:45 PM, Daniel Lee wrote:
> Thanks for the updates. It looks pretty good. I ran the test, but it's failing (I think it's the nesterov optimization
> thing you mentioned).

We can just get rid of the Nesterov optimization method
unless you think it's a good alternative to BFGS in some cases.

> I'm running a simple model, the one in src/models/command.stan. (to build: make src/models/command)
>
> Some things I've found:
>
> - init with a negative number hangs:  ./src/models/command init=-1 sample data=src/models/command.data.R
> It doesn't sample, doesn't do anything.
>
> - percentages are off for calculating iterations:  ./src/models/command sample num_warmup=10 num_samples=10
> data=src/models/command.data.R
> ...
> Iteration:  1 / 20 [  5%]  (Warmup)
> Iteration: 11 / 20 [ 55%]  (Sampling)
> ...
> Should be 0%, 50%?

Eh?  Isn't 11/20 55%?

> Was the intention to have 20/20 be [100%]?

The two options that would make sense would be 11/20 and 55%
or 1/10 and 10%.  I prefer the continuous numbering because
it gives you a better overall sense of progress.  Restarting
progress monitors is a UI no-no.  We could print the actual
number of iterations and the number of samples collected; the
latter could roll in thinning.

> - can we rename the 'diagnostic' method to a verb? The other options are verbs: 'sample' and 'optimize'.

That'd be "diagnose".  I like it.

- Bob

