> Eh?  Isn't 11/20 55%?

My understanding of the issue is that we're processing iteration 11, but it hasn't been completed yet.  So we're really only at (i - 1) / n, not i / n.  At least, that's the motivation behind the fix I pushed last night.

Also there's still the question of whether or not to force output on the last iteration as well as the first.

> That'd be "diagnose".  I like it.

No problem.  I'll push a fix in just one minute.

