The arg refactor's a go (thank Daniel for all the
testing).  Thanks for being so patient --- it takes forever
to get a lot of feedback and test, but I think it's
worth it in the end.

That's the last big ticket item for 2.0 --- there are
a few minor items that I can knock off in a day or two.
I'm waiting on a bunch of doc updates until after your
revisions.

The big to-do item for AFTER 2.0 is getting fvar<fvar<var> >
working on Windows --- the heavy templating is blowing out the
32-bit compiler that comes with RTools.  A 64-bit compile might help,
but it remains to figure out how to make it easy (or even possible)
to install.

- Bob

